Kindle Anki Port release-policy documentation alignment — 2026-08-22 UTC

Follow-on audit after QEMU-bound packaging found two documentation contracts still
encoding the obsolete package-before-QEMU order:

1. docs/TEST_ENVIRONMENT.md
   old L1 text included "unpack and audit the installation archive" while L2 was
   exact-rootfs QEMU. That implied release packaging could occur before L2.

2. testenv/README.md
   old numbered order was:
     3 run-armhf-gates.sh
     4 package-and-audit.sh
     5 run-qemu-smoke.sh
   This directly contradicted the production package gate.

Corrections:
  docs/TEST_ENVIRONMENT.md now defines:
    L0 host/deterministic
    L1 ARMHF/ABI
    L2 exact PW6 rootfs QEMU
    L2.5 QEMU-bound package/privacy/reproducibility
    L5 physical PW6 hardware acceptance

  testenv/README.md now documents:
    static -> host backend -> five real APKGs -> ARMHF -> exact-rootfs QEMU
    -> package -> durable GitHub artifacts -> separate PW6 HIL

  tests/test_build_entrypoints.py now locks both documentation contracts to the
  executable QEMU-before-package ordering so future policy drift is caught by
  run-static-gates.sh.

